From 47d220df44805e1fa6681a1a6d1a977401ef6930 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:56:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: the video scaling method says that Dolby Vision
 output does not use it

Kodi's "Video scaling method" (the video settings of the player) is read by the GLES
renderer when it draws a picture itself. The Dolby Vision bridge draws the pictures of
native Dolby Vision output, of Dolby Vision rebuilt as HDR10 or SDR and of HDR10 or HDR10+
sent as Dolby Vision: it scales the layers with libplacebo's own filters and never reads
that setting (the bridge has no reference to it), so setting it to nearest neighbour
there changes nothing, and for a picture that Kodi draws it does what it did. A user set
it to nearest neighbour for each video believing it was the scaling of the profile 7
enhancement layer. The label now ends with "(not used by Dolby Vision output)"; core 41140,
Estuary 32620, in English and in Spanish for es_es, es_ar and es_mx.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po        | 6 ++++++
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po            | 6 ++++++
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po            | 6 ++++++
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po            | 6 ++++++
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po            | 6 ++++++
 xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp            | 7 +++++++
 6 files changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 7c4147f..35d17b4 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -27238,3 +27238,9 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#41134"
 msgid "Projector"
 msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: added to the label of "Video scaling method" (video settings): the Dolby Vision output is scaled by Hades, not by this
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41140"
+msgid "(not used by Dolby Vision output)"
+msgstr ""
